# 中频词汇 List01
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023恋练有词
# 描述: 中频词汇List01核心词汇

{{abstract}}{/ˈæbstrækt/}{抽象的；摘要}{The concept of justice is quite abstract.}}
{{accelerate}}{/əkˈseləreɪt/}{加速；促进}{The government aims to accelerate economic development.}}
{{accurate}}{/ˈækjərət/}{精确的；准确的}{The report provides an accurate description of the situation.}}
{{accuse}}{/əˈkjuːz/}{指控；指责}{He was accused of stealing confidential data.}}
{{achieve}}{/əˈtʃiːv/}{实现；达到}{She achieved her goal of becoming a doctor.}}
{{addict}}{/ˈædɪkt/}{使上瘾；瘾君子}{Many teenagers are addicted to social media.}}
{{administration}}{/ədˌmɪnɪˈstreɪʃn/}{管理；行政}{The university administration approved the new policy.}}
{{adolescent}}{/ˌædəˈlesnt/}{青少年的；青少年}{Adolescent health is an important area of research.}}
{{adopt}}{/əˈdɒpt/}{采用；收养}{The company adopted a new strategy for marketing.}}
{{advanced}}{/ədˈvɑːnst/}{先进的；高级的}{The country has advanced technology in robotics.}}
{{advantage}}{/ədˈvɑːntɪdʒ/}{优势；好处}{Being bilingual is a great advantage in today's job market.}}
{{adverse}}{/ˈædvɜːs/}{不利的；有害的}{Adverse weather conditions delayed the flight.}}
{{affair}}{/əˈfeər/}{事务；事件}{The government handles foreign affairs carefully.}}
{{affect}}{/əˈfekt/}{影响；感动}{The drought severely affected crop yields.}}
{{afford}}{/əˈfɔːd/}{负担得起；提供}{Many families cannot afford quality healthcare.}}
{{agenda}}{/əˈdʒendə/}{议程；日程}{Climate change is at the top of the global agenda.}}
{{aggressive}}{/əˈɡresɪv/}{侵略性的；积极进取的}{The company has an aggressive expansion plan.}}
{{alert}}{/əˈlɜːt/}{警觉的；警报}{The system sends an alert when temperatures rise above normal.}}
{{alien}}{/ˈeɪliən/}{外星的；陌生的}{The concept felt alien to people in rural areas.}}
{{alongside}}{/əˌlɒŋˈsaɪd/}{在...旁边；与...一起}{She worked alongside experienced professionals.}}
{{alternative}}{/ɔːlˈtɜːnətɪv/}{替代的；可选择的}{We need to find alternative energy sources.}}
{{amend}}{/əˈmend/}{修改；修正}{The law was amended to include new provisions.}}
{{ample}}{/ˈæmpl/}{充足的；丰富的}{There is ample evidence to support the theory.}}
{{analogy}}{/əˈnælədʒi/}{类比；类似}{He drew an analogy between the brain and a computer.}}
{{annual}}{/ˈænjuəl/}{年度的；每年的}{The company publishes an annual report.}}
{{appeal}}{/əˈpiːl/}{呼吁；上诉；吸引力}{The charity made an appeal for donations.}}
{{appetite}}{/ˈæpɪtaɪt/}{食欲；欲望}{The scandal dampened investors' appetite for risk.}}
{{applaud}}{/əˈplɔːd/}{鼓掌；赞赏}{The audience applauded the performance enthusiastically.}}
{{apply}}{/əˈplaɪ/}{应用；申请}{These principles apply to all situations.}}
{{appoint}}{/əˈpɔɪnt/}{任命；指定}{The board appointed a new CEO last month.}}
